From: Bartlomiej Dudzik <15948633+BobrImperator@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Use Wayland as the Linux windowing and clipboard backend

`bevy_winit`'s default `x11` feature pulled the X11 backend (`x11rb`,
`x11-dl`) into every Linux application that depends on bevy_egui.
`manage_clipboard` also pulled `arboard`, whose Linux clipboard always
links `x11rb`, even with its `wayland-data-control` feature.

On Linux, select `bevy_winit` without default features and with its
`wayland` backend, and do not select `arboard` or `thread_local`.
`smithay-clipboard`, which bevy_egui already tries first when the
window runs on Wayland, becomes the only clipboard there, and the
arboard fallback compiles out. Copying an image on Linux logs the error
the smithay path already logged and does nothing.

Every other target, the BSDs included, keeps upstream's `bevy_winit`
default features and clipboard selection unchanged.
---
 Cargo.toml |  9 +++++++--
 src/lib.rs | 17 +++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Cargo.toml b/Cargo.toml
index 5d4cb7bc..3d28dc12 100644
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -105,7 +105,6 @@ bevy_reflect = { version = "0.20.0" }
 bevy_time = { version = "0.20.0" }
 bevy_shape = { version = "0.20.0" }
 bevy_window = { version = "0.20.0" }
-bevy_winit = { version = "0.20.0" }
 bevy_utils = { version = "0.20.0", features = ["debug"] }
 winit = { version = "0.30", default-features = false }
 
@@ -133,8 +132,14 @@ bevy_ui_render = { version = "0.20.0", optional = true }
 # `picking` feature
 bevy_picking = { version = "0.20.0", optional = true, features = ["mesh_picking"] }
 
+# Linux uses only the Wayland windowing backend; other targets keep `bevy_winit`'s defaults.
+[target.'cfg(target_os = "linux")'.dependencies]
+bevy_winit = { version = "0.20.0", default-features = false, features = ["wayland"] }
+[target.'cfg(not(target_os = "linux"))'.dependencies]
+bevy_winit = { version = "0.20.0" }
+
 # `manage_clipboard` feature
-[target.'cfg(not(any(target_arch = "wasm32", target_os = "android")))'.dependencies]
+[target.'cfg(not(any(target_arch = "wasm32", target_os = "android", target_os = "linux")))'.dependencies]
 arboard = { version = "3.2.0", optional = true }
 thread_local = { version = "1.1.0", optional = true }
 [target.'cfg(any(target_os="linux", target_os="dragonfly", target_os="freebsd", target_os="netbsd", target_os="openbsd"))'.dependencies]
